Hey,

after seven years of abstinence, I have started to play NetHack again. I
was a little worried that my skills have degraded considerably over this
timescale, and having to get used to the vi keys certainly didn't help
either. However, I seem to be a better NetHack player than I thought.

I started playing rogues, mostly because they have not too bad stats and
starting equipment, and can also do some spellcasting. After three
unsuccessful attempts (2x lycanthropy, 1x fire ants), I found Gauntlets
of Power early on, meaning I had a promising candidate going. Shortly
afterwards, I encountered a shop with a Shield of Reflection, making
this one even more interesting. However, after that the RNG didn't give
me any further favors, so I had to do the rest the hard way. Sokoban hat
the BoH, and after getting poison resistance I went into the mines.

The Minetown altar was cross-aligned and the shops didn't produce
anything useful. I #named an elven dagger to get Sting, mostly to
prevent it from becoming a sacrifice gift. I got the luckstone and
proceeded on my course through the main dungeon. A few levels below the
Oracle I found an altar, and some rounds of sacrificing gave me
Stormbringer and some minor artifacts, but no sign of the Foo
Brands. After having a very unfortunate encounter with a chameleon
turned titan, I decided to postpone the quest until I had either MR or a
ring of protection against shape changers. After the latter showed up, I
went cleared the quest levels. I approached the Master Assassin by
digging down from the level above, and returned with a cursed ?oT. Even
his wand of death couldn't stop me nor my daggers that toasted him in
two rounds.

Just when I was getting worried about my lack of MR, a jaguar
death-dropped an unidentified cloak, and a charge from a /oEnlightment
confirmed that this was indeed the one I was looking for. Further down,
I found a strange bones file (playing on NAO) that had three (!) magic
markers, but hardly anything else (besides Mojo and Excalibur, but I
didn't want to use them). Fort Knox also appeared somewhere around
there, and I could finally ditch my dwarven mithril coat for a black
dragon scale mail.

Since I still lacked levitation, I dug my way to the castle and
approached Medusa from below. The castle wand was at (0:1), and I
decided to burn my first wish on a GDSM, so that I could use my robe I
got when being too careless with Stormbringer near a temple priest. A
second wish went for a =oLevitation so that I could continue to clear
the castle. Happily casting magic mapping, Gehennom was not so dull as
usual. However, nothing particularly noteworthy happend until I reached
the Sanctum. There, Rodney showed up and started double troubling the
high priest. When I also got there and killed the priest, I found myself
in some trouble for the first time. The two Rodneys summoned several
spellcasters that were able to start making dents on my HPs. Eventually,
I got rid of the wizards and the rest of the pack, and swiftly rushed up
the levels. Being chaotic, the mysterious force wasn't too bad, in fact,
when it did not occur, I was worried that I might had gotten the wrong
amulet. Anyway, I ran up the dungeon, getting back my gold I lent to the
cross-aligned priest. Rodney appeared on earth the last time, and the
others were also not too exciting.

Then came Astral. I noticed that the nearest altar was guarded by Death,
and since I had less than 300 max HP, I wanted to avoid him as long as
possible. I went for the one guarded by Famine, finding it to be the
lawful one. Theoretically, I could have ended the game with a wish for a
HoOA, but I thought that I couldn't let down Kos after all he did for
me. There should be really a conduct for not changing alignment. So I
went for the altar guarded by Pestilence, and things became really
scary. He ducked so many death rays that it was hard to believe and
regularly managed to have both of his sickness attacks to succeed. And
of course, his altar was also wrong. Sigh. I waded through the hordes of
monsters and slowly moved towards the last altar only to encouter Famine
once more on my way. With my /oDeath down to one charge, I entered the
hall containing Death. At least, I managed to push my way around him
without engaging him in combat, using the ants summoned by the priests
as a fort. Finally on the right altar, I wished for a magic whistle to
call in my guardian angel and got the demigod T-shirt.

